n|kind|rows|problem|proposed fix|status
1|counterproductive|LR-3.02|"Every noun is something the reader can see, touch or count", taken literally in an argument chapter, forces made-up images (the "vague metaphor no one uses" failure)|Prefer concrete nouns, explain ideas plainly|flagged
2|counterproductive|BR-R22|"One honest limit per chapter" is a quota that invites a disclaimer, the paragraph that was cut four times|Drop the quota. Keep "hedge only at a real limit"|flagged
3|counterproductive|BR-R10, BR-R31, LR-5.19|Number quotas: short sentences "1 in 7 to 1 in 5", a heading "every 400 to 600 words", "at least one long winding sentence". The model hits the number and misses the job|Keep the job, drop the numbers (lint may report them)|flagged
4|counterproductive|BR-R12, BR-R12a|Exact parallel frames and same-frame paragraph openers. This push made round 3 "robotic and repeated", and it fights R13 (break a run)|Parallel only when items truly match. Drop R12a|flagged
5|counterproductive|BR-R16a|"Carry every case into another area of life" as a Tier 1 must adds a boilerplate "this works for X, Y, Z" paragraph after every case and fights R39. From one article|Tier 2, use it when a case is narrow|flagged
6|counterproductive|LR-5.10, LR-9.08, LR-11.05, LR-11.06, LR-11.07, LR-6.08, LR-4.03|Praised passages written as patterns (the force paragraph, "similarly:", the structural moves list, the ages series). Loud examples get copied into every draft (plan cause 6)|Move them to the style bank as examples|flagged
7|counterproductive|BR-R3, WS-16, and others|Angry quotes inside rule text make the model over-apply that one rule|Quotes go to the evidence column. The rule line stays calm|flagged
8|counterproductive|LR-3.03|A banned-word list from one draft (circuit, variable, reasonable, eventually and more). The model swaps synonyms and keeps the abstract sentence|Drop the list. The concrete-noun rule does the job|flagged
9|counterproductive|WS-20, WS-SC|Claude scores its own draft before delivery. It gave 7.5 to the epoch he nearly dropped|Blind checkers replace it. His scorecard stays|flagged
10|counterproductive|BR-R21|"Warmth is the author's own story, right after a case." With no story for that spot in the brain, the model invents biography or forces an "I, too"|Only from the brain, never a quota|flagged
11|business change|LR-3.09, LR-1.01, WS-18|Vocabulary diff against six March to May articles. The target is now book standard, and the corpus has to be rebuilt from Notion each time|His call: (a) drop it (b) keep it for articles|flagged
12|business change|LR-3.06, LR-1.05, LR-1.06, LR-11.04, WS-05|Article-only splits (digits, self-talk on its own line, 600 ballpark, readability band). Articles now feed chapters, so each split is rework later|His call: (a) one convention for everything (b) keep the splits|flagged
13|business change|LR-00d, LR-8.14, CR-00 to CR-05, MA-02, MW-02|The short-form track: [short-form] tags, storyboards, the 5x5x5 brainstorm. Its skill (content-from-article) is gone and its log is empty|His call: (a) retire it (b) keep it for a future content card|flagged
